            <ArticleTitle>Enlarged peroneal process with peroneus longus tendon entrapment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>313-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 50-year-old man was treated conservatively for chronic bilateral ankle pain for several years. Plain radiographs obtained following exacerbation of symptoms showed bilateral enlarged peroneal processes. CT and MRI demonstrated bony detail of the unusual processes and also showed isolation of the peroneus longus tendons and associated tendinitis and partial tears.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
